# Academic Efforts and Study Habits among Students in a Principles of Macroeconomics Course.

**Authors:** Okpala, Amon O., Okpala, Comfort O., Ellis, Richard

## Abstract
Students in a macroeconomics course (n=132) were compared on grade point average, academic efficacy, credit hours accumulated, and study hours/habits. Academic efficacy and study habits significantly explained achievement. The amount of study time had no significant impact. Scholastic Assessment Test scores and credit hours explained achievement of above-average but not below-average students. (SK)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ606066

